[
  {
    "file": "screen002.png",
    "sha256": "cf5068b5af7ab64cadec30e5ff65de2bd7e211e2810da36e9edf13924a88600e",
    "k": 1,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "transition",
    "en": "Now listen to part two of the interview.",
    "zh": "现在请听访谈的第二部分。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "listen"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen003.png",
    "sha256": "a176489104389c81c25579a087bc5dace2fd6a4bb783eaffbf5d366a0936ca74",
    "k": 2,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "transition",
    "en": "Questions 6 to 10 are based on part 2 of the interview.",
    "zh": "第6至10题根据访谈的第二部分提问。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "be based on"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen004.png",
    "sha256": "848807e7f3dda070e103db3e5f66e8d230b325d3a8f3f071b984aabcf38ea8d0",
    "k": 3,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "In My Poets, you write about attending readings, and socializing with writers, and the energy or tension of those face-to-face encounters.",
    "zh": "在《我的诗人》中，您写到了参加朗诵会、与作家交往，以及这些面对面接触带来的活力或紧张感。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "face-to-face"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen005.png",
    "sha256": "98881c174d589c5d7283de55fdd8b73ce8b63f10bd9b11bd8131b9be1a80559b",
    "k": 4,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "But in interviews, you've also said that you think that it’s “a tremendous gift to be lonely in poetry”.",
    "zh": "但您在访谈中也说过，对诗歌创作而言，“孤独是一份极大的馈赠”。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "tremendous"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen006.png",
    "sha256": "2865860903fd56968be22ee3ca0ea06d4ec8f9fd8ede151cfc65ec87de6d403a",
    "k": 5,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Could you talk about that?",
    "zh": "您能谈谈这一点吗？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "talk about"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen007.png",
    "sha256": "dee6e4eeef8bb2f94d048876f26a2d900ebfcb59e970c0b65de320d73643d467",
    "k": 6,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "I really think this comes down to one’s temperament.",
    "zh": "我觉得，这归根结底取决于一个人的性情。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "temperament"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen008.png",
    "sha256": "582b60d6c8dc60e10d9710fe1a4b8a48139e1f781185e8bf61262cf07441c78c",
    "k": 7,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Other writers are much more readily sociable creatures.",
    "zh": "其他作家往往更乐于社交。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "sociable"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen009.png",
    "sha256": "18a6d33faca3cb4bbdcf189cd2c13a3fb702b456490a082619f1012aa01799f4",
    "k": 8,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "They feel there’s a kind of continuity between their writing life and their social life.",
    "zh": "他们觉得，写作生活与社交生活之间存在某种连续性。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "continuity"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen010.png",
    "sha256": "6fae49bd7d1f8e04dbef1e62a0a04b060671d90403a574af56604351b81d1987",
    "k": 9,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "I never experienced things that way at all.",
    "zh": "我完全没有过那样的体验。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "experience"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen011.png",
    "sha256": "e711d5d0ba7cdafb4021afb7692329c0767cac7b4338912fdc4e42a7a582a36f",
    "k": 10,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Could you tell us why?",
    "zh": "您能告诉我们为什么吗？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "why"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen012.png",
    "sha256": "c5e5a88c67b21eee2843e51dab7b2e3efb4a9efe9caf37379f0e057a069f05e0",
    "k": 11,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "For me, poetry was not a zone about professionalization or networking.",
    "zh": "对我来说，诗歌并不是一个以职业化或建立人脉为中心的领域。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "networking"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen013.png",
    "sha256": "26146acd1ba6bb4b915761d4a858fae4b7acd759d182604a70f7d48940eef430",
    "k": 12,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "There are many, many different kinds of writerly engagement, but I feel that people should be given permission not to engage.",
    "zh": "作家与外界互动的方式有很多很多种，但我觉得，人们也应该被允许不参与其中。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "engagement"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen014.png",
    "sha256": "4ca80fe5eaff5df1bfa938e1182b3ff2259af2f380eb72366bcf707354865763",
    "k": 13,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "There’s so much pressure to find a community, and one wants a community — but community may not come from the people organizing the poetry reading.",
    "zh": "寻找一个群体的压力很大，人们也确实渴望有一个群体；但这个群体未必来自那些组织诗歌朗诵会的人。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "community"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen015.png",
    "sha256": "f37c7c7c0fcf7743f78b1defd6445490141ff141095d308fb9c1f3e9f478eb4e",
    "k": 14,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "It might be found among the folk musicians playing down there in the street.",
    "zh": "你也可能在街头演奏的民间音乐人那里找到这个群体。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "folk musician"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen016.png",
    "sha256": "a77e2f3035d31acc0dfb9e849f30d1b775823b51d9d9343db10b96c02303fc75",
    "k": 15,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "A community for poets is not necessarily other living poets.",
    "zh": "诗人的群体不一定就是其他在世的诗人。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "necessarily"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen017.png",
    "sha256": "fe1076418e14ffaf2ed7396a20e52ddd059252f347f4e7a24d9fe97f47b1bd08",
    "k": 16,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Another question.",
    "zh": "换个问题。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "question"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen018.png",
    "sha256": "969a1d220adb1c3c15d751950eda8b127321c5f7871ce4e8850a02fee0f5d437",
    "k": 17,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "How do you arrange the poetry in your books?",
    "zh": "您是怎样安排诗集中各首诗的顺序的？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "arrange"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen019.png",
    "sha256": "ae6a15ccde88a58091b33136859a1d4c5dea45f0d69606a1545d843ab9bb9d83",
    "k": 18,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "I notice that they’re all divided into sections, and all end with a concluding part.",
    "zh": "我注意到，它们都分成若干部分，而且最后都有一个结尾部分。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "divide"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen020.png",
    "sha256": "f6e3aaa88ba438e5de153e0e2b14406267461b2f177fa9a2b81b5c1d0fee71e5",
    "k": 19,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "My last two books, for instance, This Blue, have central sections that speak to a complex set of associations with particular places.",
    "zh": "比如，我最近的两本书，包括《这片蓝》，都有位于中间的部分，涉及与特定地点相关的一组复杂联想。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "association"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen021.png",
    "sha256": "065145f55ffc64685148c8d9cc0bb99e3259fe7f6c9da39c64d4b17e8dae8cf0",
    "k": 20,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "It’s also the case that some of the poems are so strongly voiced that if I were to begin with them.",
    "zh": "有些诗的声音或表达方式又特别鲜明，以至于如果我拿它们作为开篇……",
    "vocabulary": [
      "voiced"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen022.png",
    "sha256": "517c9b4372cf5af07b0d46dcaec2dab7ad2373216fd3ee27c6f85868438bf84b",
    "k": 21,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "People might think the entire book is in that one mode, and I wanted to avoid that.",
    "zh": "人们可能就会以为整本书都是那一种风格，而我想避免这种情况。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "mode"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen023.png",
    "sha256": "5d4882e400ce8edadf9e3e63eb10b19bd48dbab6db63c888fee102bc48910ec5",
    "k": 22,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "And I often write sequences.",
    "zh": "我还经常写组诗。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "sequence"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen024.png",
    "sha256": "73ff9a9f5c9ae4436731d24f8a38f58072acd7a48f1a0571042cd42500d10130",
    "k": 23,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "So I almost think of the sections more musically.",
    "zh": "所以，我几乎是在从音乐的角度思考这些部分的。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "musically"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen025.png",
    "sha256": "c229d461679ada6acaa6a641ba9647fb5e6e25d634cdb11f16887c6e5100c2d6",
    "k": 24,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Emm, Emm...",
    "zh": "嗯，嗯……",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Emm"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen026.png",
    "sha256": "41b7d956b09d9e5bb0f86f64a61682873a979194521de4356e9ae2a88915ac03",
    "k": 25,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "And I’m interested in ushering people through a series of mental and tonal landscapes, of sound- and thought-worlds.",
    "zh": "我希望引导读者走过一系列精神与声调的景观，走过声音和思想的世界。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "usher"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen027.png",
    "sha256": "ebc6d640f9e471494d26f3c0651f60696ac840ef48caf8f912065e20ad0fa937",
    "k": 26,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "For good or ill, my books have not tended to be that narrative.",
    "zh": "不论这是好是坏，我的书一直都不太偏重叙事。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "For good or ill"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen028.png",
    "sha256": "a5ce4f7b477188d9785d03c9129c63367dc2f0351c5f90031bb1ff6421eaf3e2",
    "k": 27,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Is this the reason that each section has a concluding part?",
    "zh": "这就是每个部分都设置结尾的原因吗？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "concluding"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen029.png",
    "sha256": "699ae3b4a76487ddddfa93efa34ee9fd1181ae268ee911aa10b7f0a80da49825",
    "k": 28,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "I think a concluding stanza marks a kind of “sending forth of the book” to the world.",
    "zh": "我认为，结尾的一节诗标志着一种把这本书“送入世界”的方式。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "stanza"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen030.png",
    "sha256": "59d893334b04411c63aff06fa802dae6c53a357b089d41f2171fed7c9b747834",
    "k": 29,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "It also allows you to back away from something, to modulate out of certain kinds of intensities, and to gesture maybe to something in the future.",
    "zh": "它还让你能够从某些东西中退后一步，从某种强烈的情绪中缓缓转出，并且也许向未来的某种事物作出示意。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "modulate"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen031.png",
    "sha256": "90b6ddd0a7ece25bddcbdb8a313a44c47fefc00033a5a808f64e061b16d866cb",
    "k": 30,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "It can either restate a note, or it can refer to something more broadly.",
    "zh": "它可以重申一个基调，也可以指向更广阔的内容。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "restate"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen032.png",
    "sha256": "9d7ea157b25e3e888f9ad3f274fe754b674771bf5ac74192b860c38b26e43a1f",
    "k": 31,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Do you have a particular approach to reading your own poetry aloud?",
    "zh": "您朗读自己的诗时，有没有某种特定的方法？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "approach"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen033.png",
    "sha256": "f2a37b09d39e8d7993d9f4744a5f98847d6aa931c7d623d0cfbb8599c4529df1",
    "k": 32,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Well, you can get locked into your own sense of things, and your way may not be the best way to read that poem.",
    "zh": "你可能会被自己固有的理解束缚，而你的方式未必就是朗读那首诗的最佳方式。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "get locked into"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen034.png",
    "sha256": "05116c17f97851c5dd2731bcf39bd7299a8e9ac0a721ea27d5cba817106f34b1",
    "k": 33,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "You can get a little muscular contraction on your face.",
    "zh": "你的面部可能会出现一点肌肉收缩。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "muscular contraction"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen035.png",
    "sha256": "c26b9361ecd9c7d1ef2bd2e6e11db95f33602c7e8b289ea4b438356282d8b692",
    "k": 34,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "One doesn’t want to have facial tics, one doesn’t want things to be routinized, and I think about that.",
    "zh": "人们不希望自己出现面部抽动，也不希望一切都变成固定套路，我会思考这些问题。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "facial tic"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen036.png",
    "sha256": "4799e7e013ca05425a2c88911fa9ecfaa582af15d6f798448eb64c55b641f9fa",
    "k": 35,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Sometimes people are surprised by my reading.",
    "zh": "有时候，人们会对我的朗读方式感到惊讶。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "surprise"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen037.png",
    "sha256": "e8a3e368310c1f076f2c3c8d86920bf8bb9c0503daa6a762a199bd1e6cd1e01a",
    "k": 36,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "I remember a poet said to me, “Oh, your poems are a lot funnier than I thought they were.” He was being very nice, but I didn’t know how to take that!",
    "zh": "我记得一位诗人对我说：“哦，你的诗比我想象的好笑多了。”他的态度很友善，但我当时不知道该怎么理解这句话！",
    "vocabulary": [
      "take that"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen038.png",
    "sha256": "4458d848f6a0e7544373a39dcb84a67e441bd879b68ab79a28472b33410748e7",
    "k": 37,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Ha ha ha...",
    "zh": "哈哈哈……",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Ha ha ha"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen039.png",
    "sha256": "408f7fa022d6145d72a00c0c5a2de9d280bbda41c5eb6cb641e6fb54051edaf5",
    "k": 38,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Okay.",
    "zh": "好的。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Okay"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen040.png",
    "sha256": "8c5b14da2b16e73805cd62ee6b23f06bd6e398ad74b7b8d257717c386c155705",
    "k": 39,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Maureen, thank you so much for being with us today.",
    "zh": "莫琳，非常感谢您今天参加我们的节目。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "being with us"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen041.png",
    "sha256": "84c88e37ac8d1a2a324c554b2d949f316e54124013c31e4074d53894c6e5af06",
    "k": 40,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "body",
    "en": "Pleasure.",
    "zh": "很荣幸。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "pleasure"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen042.png",
    "sha256": "d78b631fa05aad71f86d16374d4e504f96d7cd4570e42e2d7d046535d6dfb9f6",
    "k": 41,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "transition",
    "en": "This is the end of part two of the interview.",
    "zh": "访谈的第二部分到此结束。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "end"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen043.png",
    "sha256": "8e4ffcbd474fed318c86929fe9525a90ceac45266e81d621238c9198b5dfd50d",
    "k": 42,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "transition",
    "en": "Questions six to ten are based on what you have just heard.",
    "zh": "第6至10题根据你刚才听到的内容提问。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "be based on"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen044.png",
    "sha256": "96edf338171e05e34bff3257029d41a42e6dd0986b9db2959a9bbb99b9ea7c0e",
    "k": 43,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "question",
    "en": "Question 6. What did Maureen think about socializing with writers?",
    "zh": "莫琳如何看待与作家交往？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "socialize"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen045.png",
    "sha256": "cb9076598ddd87288b413628147a47730a5cfdcdb992fafec0efe08099bdf38d",
    "k": 44,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "question",
    "en": "Question 7. What was Maureen’s view about a community for poets?",
    "zh": "莫琳如何看待诗人的群体或圈子？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "community"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen046.png",
    "sha256": "2cc4bd668d19d9af8969dce2c75fc8f35325b4146ab4a5c50803626e3162f3d0",
    "k": 45,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "question",
    "en": "Question 8. Why did her sections have concluding stanzas?",
    "zh": "她为什么在各部分设置结尾的诗节？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "stanza"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen047.png",
    "sha256": "ee00083e01b61781b692e5cd36742a60fd67c5eec3f22c00806fd35ed987a03a",
    "k": 46,
